Is CTPAT’s seal verification process followed to ensure all high security seals (bolt/cable) have been affixed properly to IIT, and are operating as designed? The procedure is known as the VVTT process:
V – View seal and container locking mechanisms; ensure they are OK;
V – Verify seal number against shipment documents for accuracy;
T – Tug on seal to make sure it is affixed properly;
T – Twist and turn the bolt seal to make sure its components do not unscrew, separate from one another, or any part of the seal becomes loose. This is a requirement.

